      "artist": "AlejandraS03",
      "description": "Porto Cathedral is the seat of the diocese and one of the city's oldest and most emblematic monuments, dating back to the 12th century and undergoing continuous transformations until the 18th. Its architecture primarily combines Romanesque elements, notable for its solid floor plan, semicircular arches, and fortified walls, with later Gothic (such as the cloister) and Baroque additions.\nThe facade stands out for its church-fortress appearance, flanked by two square towers and a large Romanesque rose window beneath a crenellated arch, alongside a Baroque portico that reveals the stylistic overlaps. This blend of styles reflects the building's historical evolution and its importance as the spiritual and social center of Porto.",
